      "cml:logicSummary": "Must provide evidence on potential damage or breach of confidence",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) Before determining that the record is not an exempt record, the Tribunal must request the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security to appear personally and give evidence..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:freedom-of-information-removal-of-conclusive-certificates-and-other-measures-act-2009-sch-2-sec-50a-ss-2-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...whether making the record available for public access would constitute a breach of confidence by disclosing information or matter communicated in confidence by or on behalf of a foreign government, an authority of a foreign government or an international organisation to the Government of the Commonwealth, to an authority of the Commonwealth or to a person receiving the communication on behalf of the Commonwealth or of an authority of the Commonwealth.",
